  "provider_query": "Find the public X status from OpenAI that announces GPT-4",
  "answer": "The public OpenAI (@OpenAI) status that announced GPT-4 is from March 14, 2023:\n\n1. **OpenAI (@OpenAI)** — March 14, 2023, 17:00 UTC  \n   “Announcing GPT-4, a large multimodal model, with our best-ever results on capabilities and alignment: https://openai.com/product/gpt-4”  \n   https://x.com/OpenAI/status/1635687373060317185  \n   (~59.7k likes, ~16.0k reposts; includes video) [web:0]\n\nRelated posts from the same launch window:\n\n2. **Greg Brockman (@gdb)** — March 14, 2023, 17:00 UTC  \n   “We’re releasing GPT-4 — a large multimodal model (image & text in, text out)…”  \n   https://x.com/gdb/status/1635687252616679426 [web:3]\n\n3. **Sam Altman (@sama)** — March 14, 2023, 17:02 UTC  \n   “here is GPT-4, our most capable and aligned model yet. it is available today in our API (with a waitlist) and in ChatGPT+.”  \n   https://x.com/sama/status/1635687853324902401 [web:6]\n\n4. **Sam Altman (@sama)** — follow-up in the same thread, March 14, 2023  \n   Notes that initial training finished earlier and that release took substantial safety/alignment work.  \n   https://x.com/sama/status/1635687859494715393 [web:8]\n\n5. **Peter Welinder (@npew)** — March 14, 2023, 17:01 UTC  \n   “GPT-4 is here: our smartest and most reliable model yet!”  \n   https://x.com/npew/status/1635687624047489024 [web:9]\n\n6. **Mira Murati (@miramurati)** — March 14, 2023, 17:03 UTC  \n   “Unveiling GPT-4 — our large multimodal model…”  \n   https://x.com/miramurati/status/1635688069692293121 [web:1]\n\n7. **The Verge (@verge)** — March 14, 2023  \n   Coverage of the OpenAI announcement: https://x.com/verge/status/1635688829792268307 [web:2]\n\n8. **OpenAI research post** linked from those posts: https://openai.com/research/gpt-4 (also referenced as openai.com/product/gpt-4) [web:0] [web:13]",
